    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d752">

                <pb facs="0894" n="878" sameAs="frus:frus1947v08/pg878"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.01/11–2547: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Embassy in Costa Rica
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-11-28T19:00:00-05:00">November 28,
                            1947—7 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>382. It is not clear to Dept why Costa Rican govt feels impelled to follow action
                    mentioned urtel 549 Nov. 25.<anchor n="83"
                        xml:id="d752-f1"/> It is equally difficult to believe Betancourt would
                    participate. You may however inform Fonmin
                    that Dept would not interpret action as “hostile” to US policy although
                    definitely not in line with it. You may also inform Fonmin that in opinion this govt exchange of messages with Somoza
                    would not constitute recognition since Somoza is not technically head of state.
                    Dept does not anticipate acknowledging or sending any holiday messages to Román,
                    Somoza or any other Nicaraguan official.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d752-f1" n="83" xml:id="d752-f1-content">
                <p>The Chargé in Costa Rica replied in telegram 553, December 1, 1947, 4 p.m., as
                    follows: “Foreign Office has now informed me Acting Foreign Minister meant
                    greetings with Román and not Somoza and (2) he was mistaken concerning
                    Betancourt (817.01/12–147).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
